From 0e7c3447202d9a734359c36c349c72c97163679e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:38:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(assets): a window template, a Grok retry for a poor
 answer, and who made each asset

The asset pipeline (meshgen llm tier) had no window: a "Double Hung Vinyl Window" came back as a
flat_panel (a 6 x 10 grid of solar cells) or a box. Now:

- part_templates: `window` (outer frame filling W x H x D; double / single hung, slider,
  casement, fixed; sashes set back from the frame front, glass at mid depth, grille bars, a sash
  lock). Glass gets the glass finish by default (DEFAULT_FINISH); flat_panel's description points
  windows at it. Photo mode drops the grille and lock (the photo shows them).
- meshgen.ask: a poor answer -- none at all, or not the template the product's name needs
  (`expected_template`: window, box_appliance, cylinder_tank, ...) -- is asked once more on role
  `asset_retry` (LLM_ASSET_RETRY, default xai:grok-4.20-0309-non-reasoning); Grok's answer wins
  when it's better. `cached_chat_by` records which provider:model answered (a Groq call that
  llm.chat re-sent to xAI says xai) next to the cached answer.
- part.json asset gains made_by, template, retried and seconds (additive).
- tests/conftest.py blanks LLM_ASSET_RETRY like LLM_FALLBACK: tests opt in.

Live on :8007 (Groq keys exhausted, so llm.chat's fallback answered): three Jeld-Wen 59.5 x 47.5 in
sliders -> template window/slider by xai:grok-4.20-0309-non-reasoning, 2.1-2.6 s per call, 2.4-3.0 s
per asset.

